claimed: okay-script -- markdown files with fenced ```scala code blocks compiled and executed via the real Scala 3 (dotty) compiler API in-process. Concatenated single-compilation-unit per file (blocks share scope, REPL-like); success = compiles + runs without throwing. Library API only, no sbt-test integration yet. No custom language/runtime -- driving the real scalac. Investigated ../scalascript (unrelated: a full custom markdown-as-syntax language) for prior art, found none directly reusable.
